ser  interface  it helps in alignment and arrangement  purposes for the user interface  a out is a compose function which allows  us to arrange elements in a row column  and box  so let's understand  here we can see in this example  there is a row keyword which means these  three words hello there mate that are  written inside the row function will be  arranged horizontally  the row function allows us to arrange  the elements in a horizontal manner  so hello there and mate will be arranged  horizontally  similarly the column function  lets you arrange the elements in a  vertical manner so in this case that is  in the case of column function  hello there meet will be arranged  vertically  so this was example of layout now moving  on to the next topic which is  box  in box layout the children  are stacked over each other by default  so we have to align them to put them in  different positions or proper positions  we use the align modifier to set the  position or alignment for children  elements  as we can see in this example we have  used a line modifier and we can also see  there is alignment dot top center and  alignment dot bottom center  these are the alignment options that are  applied to the child user interface  there are total nine alignment options  let's have a look at them  first three are  alignment.topstart  alignment.top and  alignment.top center  here  alignment.topstart will align the user  interface to the top left corner  top end will align at the top right  corner  and top center will align at top center  position  next three are alignment dot center  start alignment dot center end and  alignment dot center  here center start will align the user  interface to the mid left  corner  center end will align at mid right  corner and center will be aligned at the  mid center position in between center  start and center end  x3 are alignment dot bottom start  alignment dot bottom end and alignment  dot bottom center  here  bottom start will align the user  interface to the bottom left corner  bottom end will align at the bottom  right corner and bottom center will be  aligned at the bottom center position  that is in between bottom start and  bottom end  so these were the nine possible  alignments  now coming to material design  as the name suggests it helps to improve  the appearance using the material design  styling  there are three pillars of material  design which are color  typography shape  first is  color  by using values from wrapped theme you  can easily color wherever it is needed  inside the compose graphic package there  is a color class which is used by  jetpack compose  to define material design color system  color class is used  there are 13 attributes that can be used  and those are  primary primary variant secondary  secondary variant  background surface error  on primary own secondary on background  on surface on error  and is light  each of them having different means and  is used to color wherever it is needed  then there is typography  in the material theme there are material  typography styles which are used to  style or define a type system  with the help of typograph class we can  customize font style font weight font  family letter spacing text decoration  and many more attributes  third is shape  material design allows us to define  shape for small medium and large  components as well  just like typography we can easily  create shapes  now coming to  next topic which is list and animations  the list and animations are one of the  most important thing for building an app  we have already discussed row and column  earlier  here we will discuss about lazy  composibles  lazy composibles include lazy row and  lazy column  the lazy row makes a horizontal  scrolling list  and the lazy column makes the vertical  scrolling list  in this example lazy column is used  as we can see  here lazy columns is used  that is vertical scrolling list  and this is how we add elements or items  here we are adding a single item and  here we are adding multiple items  with items there is an integer 7  which means 7 items can be added  now  just like list  animations are also very important for a  smooth and attractive user experience  there are various apis that can give you  control and help with the animation  they are  animation visibility  it is used if you are animating  appearance and disappearance  then there is animation  it is used if you want to have fine  control over animation time  then there is crossfade  it is used to switch between composables  with a crossfade animation then there is  remember infinite transition  if the animation is state-based and  happens during composition and is  infinite then this is used  next is  update transition  it is used if you are animating multiple  values simultaneously  so these were some apis that can give  you control over the animations  today we will be discussing about  cortland interview questions the 30  questions that will be covered in this  video will help you summarize every  important concepts and serves as a  perfect programming resource for kotlin  interviews  so now let's get started with an  exciting video on kotlin interview  questions but before we begin make sure  to subscribe to our youtube channel and  press the bell icon to never miss an  update from simply learn  so now let's go ahead with our first  question which  is  name some of the features which are  there in kotlin but not in java  so some of the features which are there  in kotlin but not in java are null  safety feature operator overloading core  routines range expression and smartcasts  so these are some of the  features  that make kotlin better language than  java now coming to the second question  which is what is the difference between  where and well  both where and well are used for  declaration of variables however  where is a general variable that can be  assigned several times whereas val is a  final variable that is immutable and can  only be initialized once  now moving on to the third question  which is  what are the advantages of when over  switch in kotlin  in java the word switch is used whereas  in kotlin the word when is used  when is more compact and effective than  a regular switch  and it has  superior design than switch  ven can be used both an expression and a  statement but switch cannot be used as  both  it can be used as statement but it  cannot be used as expression now moving  on to our next question which is a  multiple choice question  which of the following are the types of  constructors in kotlin  so first is parameterized and constant  constructor  option b is primary constructor and  secondary constructor option c is  default and no argument constructor and  option d is none of the above so you can  take your time in figuring out the  correct option among these four options  because i am going to say its correct  option you can pause the video and take  your time  so our correct option is option b  primary constructor and secondary  constructor are the types of constructed  in kotlin  so option b is the correct option  now moving on to our next question that  is the fifth question which is  how to get the length of the string in  kotlin  so this is also a multiple choice  question our options are a  str.length of  option b  length str  option c  str dot length and option d  str dot length of with small o  so you can take your time in figuring  out what is the correct option  meanwhile  i am going to say the correct option  so a right or correct option is  option c  str.length  so if you want to  get the length of a string in kotlin you  can use str.length  now  moving on to the next question which is  which feature allows  removing the risk of occurrence of null  pointer exception  so it is an important question as well  so  there are four options first null risk  b null safety c null pointer and d all  of the above  it is a very important question  and  now the correct option  of  this question is  null safety  null safety allows us to remove the risk  of occurrence of null pointer exception  it is a very essential feature of kotlin  language  now  moving on to the seventh question which  is  what is null safety and nullible types  in kotlin  so null safety commonly referred to as  void safety ensures that no object  references have null or void values  whereas in kotlin nullable types are  references types  that are declared by appending a  question mark to the string this  question mark is what we add at the end  of the data type to make it as nullable  now  moving on to the eighth question which  is  what is higher order function in kotlin  a higher order function accepts one or  more function as arguments and returns a  function as output  it is not like any other function  the higher order functions are  frequently combined with lambda  expression to create code that is both  compact and powerful  instead of integer string or array as a  parameter to the function  we will pass anonymous function or  lambdas in higher order function  so basically we pass a function to other  function known as higher order function  now  moving on to the ninth question which is  what is elvis operator  the null safety attribute in kotlin  allows us to assign null values to the  variables  can use if else or the always operator  to see if a value has a null value  always operator returns the first  operand and if that operand is true  otherwise evaluates and returns the  other operand  now our next question is  why  is scotland interoperable with java  so this is our  tenth question  so kotlin is compatible with java  because it uses jvm byte code  jetbrains places a strong emphasis on  kotlin's interaction with existing java  code while building compatibility  the team ensures that kotlin can  interface with existing java code easily  and thoroughly  compiling it directly to bytecode speeds  up the compilation process and  eliminates the distinction between java  and kotlin on jvm  so this is the reason kotlin is  interoperable with java now coming on to  the 11th question which is  what are the range expressions  a range is a set of values defined by  their beginning and ending points  range expression in kotlin make it  easier to iterate over a set of values  to make a range in kotlin  use the range 2 and down 2 functions  we may also define a range of values by  using the double dots operator  as we can see in the example for  i in 1 double dot 10  this will print all the elements from 1  to 10  and for 10 in  down to 1  will print all the elements from 10 to 1  in descending order  the third one is which is  4  i in 1 double dot 10 step 2  this will print  elements with a gap  now step 2 means there's a gap  so it will print elements like 1  3  5 7 9 because we have used step 2 it  will use step 3 then it will give a gap  of 2  like 1  4 like that  so on  moving on to the 12th question which is  what do you understand by data class  so data classes are the classes that are  used to hold the data or information  these data classes were previously  exclusively used to generate java codes  but with the explicit implementation of  the higher and greater collection of  properties they are now important in  kotlin as well  functions like tostring and equals are  also combined with this language  now moving on to the 13th question which  is immutable variable  so this is a multiple choice question  and the options are a variable that are  changed that can be changed b a variable  that cannot change that is read only  c a variable used for string  interpolation  d none of the above  so  we have already talked about immutable  variable  and  you can pick the correct option  now i am gonna say the correct option  so the correct option is b a variable  that cannot be changed is called  immutable variable that is the variable  that cannot be changed  now  coming on to the 14th question which is  what are co-routines  it is a very important concept  so the letters co and routine stand for  cooperation and function respectively  a core routine is a coatland feature  that can perform everything a thread can  do  while still be incredibly efficient  a core routine is a lightweight code  that doesn't require any processor  background switching and doesn't map on  native threads  so this is co routines  now let's have a look at the 15th  question which is  difference between safe calls and null  check  safe call operator is used to determine  whether a variable's value is null or  not  if it is null  null will be returned otherwise the  requested value will be returned  on the other hand  when the value of the variable is null  you can use the null check operator to  throw a null pointer exception  so this is the difference between safe  call and null check  now  coming to the 16th question which is  what are init blocks in kotlin  initializer blocks that are invoked  after the primary constructor are known  as init blocks  one or more init blocks can be found in  a class file  and they will be run in order  in kotlin it is not feasible to do any  operations in the primary constructor  instead  you must utilize the init block  so this is the init blocks in kotlin  now our next question which is the 17th  question is  what are lambda's expression  so lambdas expression are anonymous  function  that can be handled as values  meaning they can be sent as arguments to  a function  returned or used in any other way that a  normal object can be used so it can be  returned and used in any other way like  a normal object can be used  so the lambda expression has no name and  is created and assigned as a separate  variable  it doesn't have any parameters and  returns no value in the function  so this is called lambda function it is  used with higher order functions  now coming to the next question which is  what is in line function  so in line functions tell the compiler  to include the entire body of the  function wherever it is called in the  code it is used to improve the  performance of higher order function as  well as the inline function call and  inform the compiler to copy parameters  and functions  to use an inline function all you have  to do is to add the inline keyword to  the beginning of the function definition  so this is  inline function  now coming to what is null safety  so null safety is a very important  feature  the type system of kotlin is designed to  eliminate the risk of null references in  code  the type system in kotlin distinguishes  between the reference that can and  cannot hold null  so here's an example of not null  reference which will show you compiler  error  so  this is the example string equals abc  after that  the other is the example of null  reference where we have used the  question mark as we have discussed  previously  so because to allow a variable to hold  null we have to declare a variable as  nullable string with question mark  so now our next question that is the  20th question is what is late in it so  late in it is an abbreviation for late  initialization  if you don't want to initialize a  variable in the constructor and instead  want to do it later and you can  guarantee the initialization before  using it  use the late init keyword to declare  that variable  it won't start allocating memory until  it's been initialized  now our 21st question is  what is the difference between const and  well  the const keyword is used to declare  properties that are immutable by nature  that is the properties that are read  only  also the values of these properties must  be known at compile time only  now if we talk about val  for read only properties the val keyword  is also used but the mean difference  between the constant val is that the val  properties can be initialized at the  runtime also  but it is not so in case of const  coming to the 22nd question which is  what is the difference between open and  public  so open for extension  is what the open keyword indicates  the open annotation on a class is the  polar opposite of the final annotation  in java  it allows others to inherit from it  on the other hand if no visibility  modifier is specified  public is used by default which means  your declaration will be visible  everywhere  if nothing else is supplied public is  used by default  so next question is  what defines a sealed class in kotlin  so it is a multiple choice question  a  it's another name for abstract class  b  it represents this restricted class  hierarchies  c it is used in every kotlin program  d  none of the above  the correct option is option b  it represents restricted class  hierarchies  so the restricted class hierarchies  defines the seed class in kotlin  now moving on to the 24th question which  is what is lazy initialization in kotlin  so lazy initialization is a feature in  kotlin that indicates that your variable  will not be initialized unless you  utilize it in your code  if it only be initialized once  after that you repeat the process with  the same value  so now moving on to our 25th question  which is what is the entry point of  every kotlin program  every kotlin program's entry point is  the main function  the main function does not have to be  written inside the class in kotlin  the jvm automatically encapsulates it in  a class when it is compiled  the command line arguments are retrieved  using the strings given in the form of  array string  so this was the answer of this question  now moving on to the next question which  is what are companion objects in kotlin  so if we wish to write a function or a  member of a class that may be called  without needing the class instance  we can do so as a member of companion  object within the class in kotlin  as a result by declaring the companion  object  we can only access the class member by a  class name  so this was the answer of companion  objects in kotlin now moving on to the  27th question 